# Optional. The fixture demo needs NO keys and must never fail without one.
# Every variable below, with what it does and its default, is tabulated in WEB.md ("Live mode").
#
# Live mode: the MEASURED model — the chatbot under test. OpenAI Responses API with the web_search
# tool, which tool_choice REQUIRES on every measured call: an ungrounded answer is excluded from the
# score, so paying for one is paying for nothing. search_executed is still read from the response's
# web_search_call item, never assumed.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# The model that ANSWERS the questions (default gpt-5.6-luna: web search, 2026 knowledge, a tenth of
# gpt-4.1's input price). LIVE_MODEL is no longer read.
MEASURED_MODEL=
# The buyer budget, spent on distinct questions rather than repeats: BUYER_QUESTIONS per front asked
# once each (default 12), REPEAT_SAMPLE of them (default 2) also asked BUYER_TRIES times (default 3)
# so the report can say how much one question wobbles between asks.
BUYER_QUESTIONS=
REPEAT_SAMPLE=
BUYER_TRIES=

# The same key drives onboarding (/api/onboard reads a company's own pages and extracts what they
# claim) and therefore every measurement of an onboarded company: crawled companies have no authored
# answers to replay, so there is no offline path for them. The two bundled scenarios still run with
# no key at all.
# Both default to gpt-4.1-mini: gpt-4o-mini's quotes were too often not verbatim to be kept.
ONBOARDING_MODEL=
EVALUATOR_MODEL=

# EVALUATOR_MODEL is the separate model that labels those answers (agents/evaluator_model.py). Set
# it to something other than MEASURED_MODEL: a model grading its own output has a self-preference bias.
# Every label it returns is still validated by code — a quote that is not verbatim is dropped.
#
# Never commit a real .env (it is gitignored). Secrets are never written to runs or exports.
